  "notes": "{取|と}りこぼす means to drop something or miss an opportunity.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nUSAGE:\nCommonly used in sports contexts when a favored team loses to a weaker opponent, or when discussing missed opportunities in business or life.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {試合|しあい}を{取|と}りこぼす: to drop a game\n- チャンスを{取|と}りこぼす: to miss a chance\n- {勝|か}ち{星|ぼし}を{取|と}りこぼす: to let a win slip away",
